+# Release 1 acceptance ledger
+
+This ledger maps every P0 and P1 requirement, every non-functional clause and all 17 acceptance scenarios of [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) to evidence or to an explicit open blocker. Its structure follows the advisor ruling in [s5-advisor-r.md](handoff/evidence/s5-advisor-r.md) (Q5).
+
+**Release verdict: NO-GO.** Linux compiles and passes its automated tests in a container (S6-NATIVE-LINUX-N31) but has never run on a Linux desktop or GPU, the Windows installers have not been executed, the provider-token scenarios (CivitAI, gated Hugging Face, Google Drive quota) are open, Authenticode signing and updater key custody are unresolved, and further Windows native scenarios are open. See [Release gates](#release-gates).
+
+## How to read this ledger
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `PASS` | The clause has the required automated evidence and, where it needs one, a native run on every platform in scope, with no open gap. |
+| `PARTIAL` | Implemented, with automated evidence and/or native evidence for some clauses, platforms or profiles. The remaining gap is named. |
+| `FAIL` | Evidence shows the clause does not hold. |
+| `OPEN` | The acceptance evidence the clause needs does not exist yet. The implementation may exist. |
+| `ACCEPTED RESIDUAL` | A known gap that an approved ruling accepts for Release 1. It is never a pass. |
+| `OWNER DECISION` | The outcome depends on a decision reserved to the owner. |
+
+"Automated" means a default-discovered Rust or Vitest test that ran green in the final check run ([S6-AUTO-WIN-007](#automated-and-packaging-evidence), 802 Rust tests, 202 Vitest tests). "Native" means a run of the real application or a real external tool on the development machine, recorded in [s6-native-register.md](handoff/evidence/s6-native-register.md) (N1–N29) or [s5-native-register.md](handoff/evidence/s5-native-register.md). Release 1 covers Windows x64 **and** Linux x64, so a requirement with Windows evidence only is at most `PARTIAL`.
